{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: lane A, the Room. Implement the Room Durable Object and its Worker entry against the approved contract (docs/protocol.md on main), hosting admission, the signed log, roster and authority, leases and subscriptions, and integrating the policy runtime (lane C) and the git/landing engine (lane B) through narrow interfaces.","body":{"conditions":"A room package (Worker + SQLite Durable Object) implementing the contract's normative rules that belong to the Room: R-ID, R-SIG (canonical bytes and Ed25519 verification), R-GEN (genesis, recovery key), R-ADM including R-ADM-12 custody by trusted admission path, R-IDEM (byte-identical replay returns the original receipt; key reuse with a different payload is refused), R-CRED and R-WS (public workspace ops; holder-only workspaceToken), R-LANE and R-PROP (generations, expectedGeneration, leases with alarm-driven expiry and fencing), R-OBL, R-LOG (acyclic sealing order, notified entries, checkpoints, publishedThrough), R-REV, R-ADMIN (including configuration-recovery lanes), and R-SEC (secret scanning before recording); the RoomWire RPC, the HTTPS routes and the WebSocket/long-poll subscription with cursors. Policy evaluation calls lane C's package (on its branch until it lands; a thin adapter so it can be swapped); landing calls lane B's engine through its interface (on its branch until it lands). Tests: every normative acceptance case in protocol.md section 23 that belongs to the Room, under workerd (vitest-pool-workers) with real SQLite, plus Node unit tests for pure parts; concurrent admission tests showing gapless sequence and fencing. README in plain English per ISO 24495-1.","target_head":"6bc755b4bef2c12e7c3ca2d62b93087f31c482bd","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}